	"web_text": "Referred to as ukpaga, this woman's ceremonial cloth is offered at marriage, carried at ceremonial events throughout a woman's life, and ultimately used as her shroud at death.Woven in two panels with intricate rows of slit-tapestry weaving and patterned in both a delicate stitch-resist and a bound-resist process, the ukpaga is distinct within the tradition of Nigerian stitch-resist dyeing.",
	"didactic_label": "Referred to as ukpaga, this woman's ceremonial cloth is offered at marriage, carried at ceremonial events throughout a woman's life, and ultimately used as her shroud at death.\nWoven in two panels with intricate rows of slit-tapestry weaving and patterned in both a delicate stitch-resist and a bound-resist process, the ukpaga is distinct within the tradition of Nigerian stitch-resist dyeing.",
